1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
7 in 100 small-business leads became customers. They waited 17.6 days, and called three times to ask where their order was.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,500
7 in 100 small-business leads became customers. They waited 17.6 days, and called three times to ask where their order was. Watch Anita, who runs an insurance agency in Visakhapatnam, do it in one sitting, on her phone.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:16,000
Anita opens Dukaan Connect on her phone. Ten Indian languages; she picks Telugu.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,900
She describes her business as she would to a person. Voice works too; here she types.

5
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:26,950
Understood: insurance agency, 25 staff, Visakhapatnam, 1 Gbps internet and email. One question left: her GSTIN.

6
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:32,950
One registry lookup fills in the business. Then one bundle, with a reason for every product, in Telugu.

7
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:37,950
Clinic & Office Pro, Rs 8,758 a month. She asked for 1 Gbps; Biz Fibre 1G is sold only in tier-1 cities, so she gets Biz Fibre 300.

8
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:45,950
What was understood, what the rules engine chose, and the rule behind every refusal. The AI talks; it never picks a product or a price.

9
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:50,450
One monthly price, on a ledger she already knows how to read. Every line says why it is there.

10
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:52,950
Add-ons tick on and off.

11
00:00:52,950 --> 00:00:56,450
She adds backup internet. The price updates at once, re-priced on the server.

12
00:00:56,450 --> 00:01:00,450
A 24-month contract brings it down to Rs 8,607 a month, plus GST.

13
00:01:00,450 --> 00:01:01,650
Her mobile number, for updates. Then: place order.

14
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:05,150
Before any KYC: a notice in her language, with one switch per purpose.

15
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:07,150
Every screen works in all ten languages. Switching to English for the judges.

16
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:11,150
Verifying and installing are needed. Order updates and offers are optional, and offers start off.

17
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:14,650
She allows order updates. Each choice is recorded with its notice version and can be withdrawn in one tap.

18
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:18,650
Registries first. The photos only confirm what the registries say.

19
00:01:18,650 --> 00:01:22,150
The GSTIN checks out against the registry: Kaveri Insurance Advisors, Proprietorship, Active.

20
00:01:22,150 --> 00:01:25,150
Four document photos, read by OCR on our own servers. For the demo, the official specimen photos of applicant K09.

21
00:01:25,150 --> 00:01:31,150
Each document is read and matched: names, address, dates. Identifiers stay masked on screen.

22
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:37,150
14 checks passed: GSTIN checksum and registry status, legal name, a bill from the last 90 days, the signatory's SIM-swap check.

23
00:01:37,150 --> 00:01:43,650
Another applicant, Trinity Bake House: the electricity bill is 257 days old. She gets a fix she can do alone, not a rejection.

24
00:01:43,650 --> 00:01:47,150
Only that one photo needs retaking; everything else stays verified.

25
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:50,650
Back to Anita. The first month by UPI Autopay.

26
00:01:50,650 --> 00:01:53,150
Paid. The mandate covers each month's bill from now on.

27
00:01:53,150 --> 00:01:55,650
She picks an installation slot that suits her.

28
00:01:55,650 --> 00:02:01,150
Cloud services go live at once; fibre is dated from the catalogue's install times. Customers who chased five times churned at 27.9%.

29
00:02:01,150 --> 00:02:05,150
When the engineer finishes, a WhatsApp message: everything is live. No calls needed.

30
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:09,150
From the same screen she can withdraw any consent, or download or erase her data.

31
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:15,650
Leads the journey did not close, ranked by a propensity score (AUC 0.71), with why each stalled and the next action.

32
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:19,150
Calls go through a masked number: partners never see the customer's phone.

33
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:22,650
KYC exceptions land here. Trinity Bake House is already fixing her own bill.

34
00:02:22,650 --> 00:02:27,150
Every pilot metric against last quarter's baseline, computed from the data.

35
00:02:27,150 --> 00:02:32,650
28 rules-engine scenarios, run live: tier-only products, staff and site minimums, cancelled GSTINs, dependencies, budgets.

36
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:39,150
All 12 specimen applicants through the real OCR: six planted defects caught, six clean applicants passed, no false rejections.

37
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:50,150
One sitting on a phone, in the owner's language.
